jobrunner 2.9.4
===============

A pool of worker threads that runs background jobs from Redis queues.

Files
-----
/etc/jobrunner/jobrunner.yml   pool size, Redis, the application, the database the jobs use
/etc/jobrunner/limits.yml      per-queue concurrency limits (the file named by limits_file)
/var/log/jobrunner/            the log
/opt/jobrunner/jobrunner.py    the daemon

The application (the file named by `app`) declares the queues and the job classes. Producers put jobs on a
queue; the queue of a job class is chosen by the application, not by jobrunner.

The pool
--------
pool.concurrency is the number of worker threads. A worker runs one job at a time. All queues share the
pool: a worker takes the next job from whichever queue has one. A change of pool.concurrency needs a
restart of the service.

Limits
------
limits.yml holds one mapping:

    limits:
      <queue name>: <number>

The number is the most jobs of that queue that may run at the same time. The queue name is compared with
the names the application declares, character for character; `jobrunnerctl queues` prints those names and
the limit in effect for each.

  - A queue that has no entry is not limited: its jobs may take every worker of the pool.
  - 0 pauses the queue: its jobs stay queued.
  - An entry whose name is not a queue of the application is skipped.

`service jobrunner reload` (SIGHUP) reads the limits file again. Jobs that are already running finish; a
lower limit takes effect as they do. If the file cannot be read, the previous limits stay in effect and
the reason is written to the log.

Failed jobs
-----------
A job whose function raises an error goes back to the front of its queue and is tried again. The worker
that ran it pauses for a moment before it takes the next job.

Restarts
--------
A job taken from a queue is kept in the Redis list `jobrunner:inflight` until it is finished. On stop the
pool waits up to 12 seconds for running jobs. Whatever is still in that list when jobrunner starts is
returned to its queue first. Jobs are written to be safe to run twice.

Tools
-----
jobrunnerctl queues     queues: jobs waiting, jobs in flight, limit in effect
jobrunnerctl status     the pool
